  "description": "Phase 2a (Full planning permission) to include the construction\nof new dwellings to provide residential homes (Use Class C3), along with cycle\nand vehicle parking, highway and access improvements, children’s play space,\npublic realm enhancements and associated landscaping (\"the\nDevelopment\").The proposal provides 2no. new buildings (Block A &amp; Block\nB) at 3-4 storeys in height. Building A is proposed at three storeys and\nBuilding B is proposed at four storeys. 45no. units (Use class C3) (18no x\n1b2p, 18no x 2b4p, 7no x 3b5p, 2no x3b6p), including the provision of 5no. part\nM4(3) homes for wheelchair users. 100% affordable homes comprising, 36no. units\n(80% provided for social rent) and 9no. units (20% provided as London Living\nRent).32no. car parking spaces provided including 5no.\naccessible disabled parking bays.&nbsp; A total of 92no. long-stay and 4no.\nshort-stay cycle parking spaces will be provided in dedicated cycle stores.Block A would incorporate x3 1,100litre bin for general\nwaste, x3 1,100litre bin for recycling and x2 240litre bin for food waste.Block B would incorporate x4 1,100litre bin for general waste,\nx4 1,100litre bin for recycling and x3 240litre bin for food waste.30no. new trees are to be planted on site.The amount of hard landscape on the Site is 2,823sqm and there\nis 2,804sqm of hard landscape proposed in total. The amount of existing soft\nlandscaping in the scheme is 2,368sqm with 2,191sqm proposed.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n683sqm of publicly accessible open space is proposed.\n145sqm of playable space is provided at ground floor level (77sqm for\n5–11-year-olds&nbsp;and 68sqm for 0–4year-olds.)",
